  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Mollicellin N may be involved in the biological process leading to the activation of HEC-1. This is supported by multiple pathways where Mollicellin N is linked to 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which in turn targets HEC-1. Additionally, Mollicellin N is also associated with P2X purinoceptor 7, which is targeted by palmarumycin CP18, another compound that ultimately affects HEC-1. These findings indicate that Mollicellin N may act through different molecular mechanisms to influence HEC-1, potentially through the activation of signaling pathways involving lipid metabolism and purinoceptor signaling. The scores from the different paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in the relationship, but further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the direct interaction between Mollicellin N and HEC-1."
